          deckDescription: 'The standard 56-card Rook pack without the Rook bird card: four colours (commonly black, red, green, yellow), each with fourteen cards numbered 1 through 14. Used for Tuxedo and other Rook-based games where capture is by matching number or by pairs that sum to 14.',
          suitDescription: 'Four Rook colours (often black, red, green, yellow), each comprising fourteen cards; colours function like suits but are not the standard French suits. Cards of the same numeric value across different colours can match for capture in Tuxedo.',
          rankDescription: 'Numeric values 1 through 14 in each of the four colours; in Tuxedo, capture is by playing a card that matches the number of a face-up card or that forms a sum of 14 with it (e.g. 5 and 9, 6 and 8).',
